  "description": "redundancy.v1 §2.9: an incumbent own, its interface's election, and the holders of the interface's token at the address in two reads a grace apart, first then second (each a set: a holder listed twice is one) -> whether it steps down. The first of: election \"external\" -> stays, external (§2.11); own not among the second read's holders -> stays, not_holding; fewer than two holders in either read -> stays, no_split; the second read's lowest holder lower than own (ids compared as their digits, §2.3) -> steps down, naming that lower holder; otherwise stays, lowest. A read's completeness plays no part: a read cannot invent a holder, so a read not complete counts the holders it shows, and one through a session cut off shows none."
